\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces System architecture. The top row is the acquisition path on the vehicle; the middle row is the training pipeline built on the carOBD corpus; the bottom row is the inference path that scores recordings and drives the dashboard.}}{10}{figure.caption.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The column-shift defect seen through one PID. Left: under a bare \texttt {read\_csv}, the TIMING\_ADVANCE column contains a large population far outside the $\pm $64$^{\circ }$ OBD-II bound (dashed lines), peaking at 776.6$^{\circ }$ --- catalyst temperatures wearing the wrong column name. Right: with \texttt {index\_col=False} the same files yield $-24^{\circ }$ to $+35^{\circ }$, entirely inside the physical range. Note the logarithmic count axis.}}{13}{figure.caption.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Fixed-holdout confusion matrix for the six-class XGBoost classifier (sessions drive1 + live12; macro-F1 = 0.962).}}{22}{figure.caption.7}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Corpus composition on both axes. By file count the idle family dominates (47 of 129); by 60-second windows, cruise dominates (62.9\,\%) because driving sessions are far longer than idle ones.}}{23}{figure.caption.8}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Distributions of the five key fault-bearing PIDs across all 129 files. Fuel trims are roughly symmetric and slightly rich-shifted with visible OBD-II quantization; coolant is bimodal (cold-start shoulder plus a warm-operation peak near 88--90$^{\circ }$C); MAP is multimodal from the idle/driving mixture; timing sits entirely inside its physical envelope.}}{23}{figure.caption.9}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Correlation heatmap of the 14 working PIDs over the full corpus.}}{24}{figure.caption.10}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Bivariate structure, colored by a row-level regime proxy. Left: MAP vs RPM separates the idle cluster from the driving cloud --- the region the air-system fault perturbs. Center: RPM vs speed resolves into discrete gear bands, a drivetrain sanity check that a residual column shift would scramble. Right: timing advance climbs and stabilizes as coolant warms --- the coupling the coolant-sensor fault exploits.}}{25}{figure.caption.11}%
